		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4473&amp;p=35981#p35981"><![CDATA[
I recently had this fault with my MD9600. I soldered a cable with a mono 3.5mm plug directly to the internal speaker and passed it out the back through a spare grommet so I can now switch between internal and external speakers again. <br>This is a v5 unit so a shame to see TYT hasn’t dealt with this problem since V1.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8179">M7JUZ</a> — Thu Feb 27, 2025 5:07 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
