		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4473&amp;p=33442#p33442"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>While playing with external speakers, I inserted a plug into the external speaker jack whose tip turned out to be a little larger diameter than it should have been. At which point the internal speaker stopped working when no plug was inserted. The speaker itself is OK, I tested it. External speakers also work fine. So probably the bad plug bent the make/break contacts for the internal speaker too far, so now they are always open.<br><br>Unfortunately, the jack is encased in black plastic. So getting at the contacts to bend them back into place is problematic. Can anyone suggest a fix? Or provide a source for a replacement jack that will fit the circuit board?<br><br>The radio is Version 1. Thanks for any help.</div></blockquote>There are some old schematic kicking around on the web.  But they may not be 100% accurate for the newer radios.<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2683&amp;sid=830c68dfade59c62fae634c0a4409e4d" class="postimage" alt="md9600_audio_amp.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Oct 11, 2024 11:33 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
