		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4473&amp;p=33441#p33441"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Broken external speaker jack]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4473&amp;p=33441#p33441"><![CDATA[
While playing with external speakers, I inserted a plug into the external speaker jack whose tip turned out to be a little larger diameter than it should have been. At which point the internal speaker stopped working when no plug was inserted. The speaker itself is OK, I tested it. External speakers also work fine. So probably the bad plug bent the make/break contacts for the internal speaker too far, so now they are always open.<br><br>Unfortunately, the jack is encased in black plastic. So getting at the contacts to bend them back into place is problematic. Can anyone suggest a fix? Or provide a source for a replacement jack that will fit the circuit board?<br><br>The radio is Version 1. Thanks for any help.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2447">KD7MW</a> — Fri Oct 11, 2024 10:28 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
